From a51970cdb94fa4a8d8577613fe5bae870bf0dc20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 22:48:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input: usb_kbd_hid: keep polling after a transient poll error

usb_kbd_poll() returned early on any poll error other than -EAGAIN.
This skipped the poller_call_async() reschedule at exit, so the
keyboard poller died permanently after a single transient error.

A control endpoint stall self-clears on the next SETUP packet. The
poller does not need to do anything special to recover. It just
needs to keep running.

Observed on hardware: kbd-hid poll failed once with -EPIPE right
after reaching the barebox prompt. The keyboard then stopped
responding for the rest of the boot.

Fix: goto exit instead of returning, so the poller reschedules
itself like the -EAGAIN case already does.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index 4649e13cf9..28cd7075da 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -111,5 +111,5 @@ static void usb_kbd_poll(void *arg)
 		dev_err(&usbdev->dev,
 			"usb_submit_int_msg() failed. Keyboard disconnect?\n");
-		return;
+		goto exit;
 	}
 
